### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 06 - REFLEX COMMANDS (ZERO-TOKEN FAST PATH)
###
### The ReflexRegistry intercepts specific input patterns BEFORE
### the LLM is ever invoked. Zero LLM tokens consumed.
### All work identically via REST (goal string) or Telegram.
###
### Reflex map (intercepted by CommandDispatchHandler → ReflexRegistry):
###   /status        → StatusReflex    - checkpoint state + USD spent
###   /halt          → HaltReflex      - emergency stop, wipe workspace
###   /reset         → ResetReflex     - soft reset (clears ReAct, keeps chat)
###   /history       → HistoryReflex   - recent chat + compaction summaries
###   /crons         → ListCronsReflex - list scheduled tasks (user-scoped)
###   /cron          → ListCronsReflex - alias for /crons
###   /list crons    → ListCronsReflex - natural language alias
###   /skills        → SkillReflex     - list loaded skills (zero token)
###   /mcp           → McpReflex       - show MCP connection status (zero token)
###   /approve       → ApproveReflex   - approve AWAITING_APPROVAL checkpoint
###   /deny          → DenyReflex      - deny AWAITING_APPROVAL checkpoint
###   deletecron <id>→ DeleteCronReflex- delete cron job by ID (also: deletecron all, /deletecron)
###   store KEY=VAL  → VaultStoreHandler- store secret (bypasses PII scan)
###   /sessions      → SessionsReflex  - list active sessions with indices
###   /newsession    → NewSessionReflex- create a new session via reflex
###   /resume <n>    → ResumeReflex    - resume session by index
###   /reflex        → ListReflexesReflex- list all registered reflexes
###   /reflexes      → ListReflexesReflex- alias for /reflex
###   /commands      → ListReflexesReflex- alias for /reflex (command reference)
###   /help          → ListReflexesReflex- alias for /reflex (help text)
###
### NOTE: PiiScanReflex and PromptInjectionReflex are automatic (triggered by
### content patterns, not explicit commands). Tested in 07_pii_prompt_injection.http.
### /github commands are handled by CommandDispatchHandler → agent tools, not reflexes.
###
### PiiScanReflex and PromptInjectionReflex are covered in 07_pii_prompt_injection.http
###
### Prerequisites: Amsha Agent serve mode
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# @baseUrl  = http://localhost:8080
# @validKey = key-ci-changeme

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SETUP: Create a shared session for reflex tests
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [REFLEX-0] Create session for reflex tests
# @name reflexSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# /STATUS - checkpoint state + budget
# StatusReflex queries StatefulAgentStore, GovernanceLayer, CompactionSummaryRepository.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [REFLEX-1] /status on fresh session - no checkpoint yet
# Expect 200: "No active session found" or budget=$0.00
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{reflexSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/status",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### Run a quick agent task first so /status has something to show
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{reflexSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "What is 1 + 1?",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [REFLEX-2] /status after an agent run - shows COMPLETED + cost
# Expect 200: COMPLETED status + token counts + USD cost > $0
# Phase 64-A A1: budget tracking now correct (hard limit before soft warning).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{reflexSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/status",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# /HISTORY - recent chat + compaction summaries
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [REFLEX-3] /history - view conversation history
# Expect 200: formatted list of recent messages. Compaction summaries if compacted.
# History is session-scoped - you only see your own messages.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{reflexSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/history",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# /RESET - soft reset (wipes ReAct checkpoint, keeps chat memory)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [REFLEX-4] /reset - clear ReAct state
# Expect 200: "🧹 Session wiped. Memory and tool states cleared."
# ReAct checkpoint is CLEARED. ChatMemoryStore is PRESERVED.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{reflexSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/reset",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [REFLEX-5] /status after reset - checkpoint cleared, budget retained
# Expect 200: NO_ACTIVE_STATE (checkpoint wiped) but cost > $0 (budget survives reset).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{reflexSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/status",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [REFLEX-5a] Chat memory survives reset
# The fact from before /reset must still be recalled.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{reflexSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "What was the first math question I asked you in this session?",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{reflexSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run-async
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/approve",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# /CRONS, /CRON, /LIST CRONS - list scheduled tasks (no LLM)
# All three aliases call ListCronsReflex → AgentCronRepository.findByUserId()
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [REFLEX-0b] Create dedicated session for cron reflex tests
# @name cronRefSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [REFLEX-6] /crons - list all scheduled tasks (alias 1)
# Expect 200: "No scheduled tasks found." or formatted list with IDs
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronRefSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/crons",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [REFLEX-7] /cron - alias 2 (identical behaviour)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronRefSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/cron",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [REFLEX-8] /list crons - natural language alias (identical behaviour)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronRefSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/list crons",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DELETECRON - delete a specific cron job by ID
# Matches: input.startsWith("deletecron")
# Tenant-isolated: user can only delete their own cron jobs.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [REFLEX-9] deletecron with non-existent ID → "not found" error
# Expect 200: "❌ Cron job 00000000-dead-beef-0000-000000000000 not found."
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronRefSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "deletecron 00000000-dead-beef-0000-000000000000",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# /SKILLS - list loaded skills (zero token, no LLM call)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [REFLEX-10] /skills - list all currently loaded skills
# Expect 200: formatted list of skill names + trigger patterns.
# "No skills currently loaded" if SkillRegistry is empty.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronRefSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/skills",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# /MCP - MCP connection status (zero token, no LLM call)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [REFLEX-11] /mcp - show MCP status
# Expect 200:
#   "Exposed internal tools (3): github, recall_memory_search, archival_memory_search
# After connecting a server via 12_mcp.http, dynamic tools appear here.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronRefSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/mcp",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VAULT KEY=VALUE - vault store
# ReflexRegistry bypasses ALL sanitization for "store" prefix messages.
# PII scan does NOT run on store commands (prevents false JWT redaction).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [REFLEX-12] vault KEY=VALUE - vault secret storage
# Expect 200: "✅ Secret 'TEST_KEY' stored securely."
# Audit event: VAULT_STORE
# Confirm in logs: NO [PII-REDACTED] line for this message.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronRefSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "store TEST_KEY=test_value_abc123",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}


###


POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronRefSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run-async
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/approve",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}


###

### [REFLEX-12a] store with JWT-like value - PII scan must NOT redact
# A raw JWT would normally trigger [REDACTED-JWT] in PiiScanReflex.
# store command bypasses PII scan entirely - JWT stored verbatim.
# Expect: "✅ Secret 'JWT_TOKEN' stored securely." - NO redaction.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronRefSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "store JWT_TOKEN=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJ0ZXN0In0.SflKxwRJSMeKKF2QT4fwpMeJf36POk6yJV_adQssw5c",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###


POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronRefSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run-async
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/approve",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}


###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# /HALT - emergency stop
# HaltReflex calls WorkspaceManager.terminateSession() immediately.
# The halted session cannot be resumed - must create a new session.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [REFLEX-13] /halt on cronRefSession - terminates it
# Expect 200: "🛑 System Halted. Workspace terminated."
# Audit event: CHECKPOINT_FAILED with reason "HALT"
# WARNING: cronRefSession is now terminated - do not reuse it.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronRefSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/halt",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [REFLEX-14] Status after halt → SESSION_NOT_FOUND
# Workspace is wiped. Checkpoint lookup finds nothing.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronRefSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [REFLEX-15] New session works after halt (bot is not affected, only workspace)
# @name postHaltSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{postHaltSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Say: System fully operational after halt.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{postHaltSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# APPROVE / DENY via goal string (in-band reflex path)
# Sending "/approve" or "/deny" as the goal triggers ApproveReflex / DenyReflex.
# These are tested more completely in 05_hitl_governance.http.
# Here we just confirm the reflex pattern matches.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [REFLEX-16] /approve on session with no pending approval → error response
# Expect 200: "No pending approval found" or equivalent.
# (Not 500 - the reflex handles missing state gracefully.)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{reflexSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/approve",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [REFLEX-17] /deny on session with no pending approval → error response
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{reflexSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/deny",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# /SESSIONS - list active sessions with indices (SessionsReflex)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [REFLEX-18] /sessions - list active sessions
